<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Adaptive icon: the launcher applies its own mask and scale, so the 108dp
    art carries 66dp of live area plus safe padding.

    No <monochrome> layer on purpose. The foreground is a multi-hue stroke
    design (cyan + purple shield and mesh paths on transparent), so tinting it
    into one colour yields a muddy silhouette on Android 13+ themed launchers
    rather than a better one. A real monochrome variant needs redrawn art,
    which belongs in a design pass, not here. The MonochromeLauncherIcon lint
    warning is the price of that decision.

    Lives in mipmap-anydpi-v26, not mipmap-anydpi. The unqualified form is
    legal for aapt2 compile but the AGP link step drops it, so the manifest
    reports "resource mipmap/ic_launcher not found". The -v26 qualifier trips
    ObsoleteSdkInt (minSdk is 31) — an informational warning, and cheaper than
    a missing launcher icon.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground" />
</adaptive-icon>
